Complete Overview of the Panchakarma Management System
The Panchakarma Management System is a web-based healthcare application developed to digitize and streamline the complete Panchakarma treatment process in Ayurvedic clinics. The system replaces traditional paper-based management by providing a centralized platform for handling patient registration, consultation scheduling, therapy planning, therapy session management, recovery tracking, pharmacy operations, and treatment history. It improves operational efficiency, reduces manual errors, and enables secure access to patient records.
The application supports four user roles: Admin, Patient, Therapist, and Pharmacist. The Admin manages users, therapy types, medicines, and overall system activities. Patients can register, book consultations, choose whether to proceed with therapist-recommended therapies, schedule therapy sessions, track their treatment journey, monitor recovery, and interact with the AI chatbot. Therapists conduct consultations, create personalized therapy plans, schedule therapy sessions, record recovery assessments, and monitor patient progress. Pharmacists manage medicine inventory, process prescriptions, and dispense medicines.
The system is developed using a modern three-tier architecture. The frontend is built with React.js and Tailwind CSS, providing responsive and role-based dashboards. The backend is implemented using Spring Boot, which manages business logic, REST APIs, authentication, authorization, and communication with the database and AI services. PostgreSQL is used as the relational database to store patient records, consultations, therapy plans, prescriptions, recovery assessments, and treatment history. Secure authentication is implemented using Spring Security and JWT (JSON Web Token) with Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
A major feature of the project is the AI-Based Recovery Prediction Module. The module uses a machine learning model based on HistGradient Boosting/XGBoost to predict a patient's expected recovery percentage using clinical parameters such as age, gender, medical condition, therapy type, completed sessions, pain level, sleep quality, energy level, and overall condition. The trained model achieved an R² Score of 99.2%, MAE of 1.15%, and RMSE of 1.77%, providing highly accurate recovery predictions. The prediction is displayed on the therapist dashboard to support treatment monitoring and clinical decision-making.
The project also integrates an AI-powered Ayurveda Chatbot based on the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approach. The chatbot uses SentenceTransformers to convert user queries into embeddings, FAISS for retrieving relevant information from an Ayurveda knowledge base, and the Google Gemini API to generate accurate, context-aware responses. It answers questions related to Panchakarma therapies, Ayurvedic concepts, diet plans, lifestyle recommendations, and wellness, improving patient awareness and engagement.
The AI services are implemented as a separate FastAPI microservice, allowing the machine learning model and chatbot to operate independently of the main application. This modular architecture improves scalability, maintainability, and future extensibility while ensuring secure communication between the React frontend, Spring Boot backend, PostgreSQL database, and AI components.

Overall, the Panchakarma Management System combines modern web technologies with Artificial Intelligence to provide a secure, scalable, and intelligent healthcare platform. It enhances treatment management, supports therapists with predictive insights, improves patient engagement through AI assistance, and contributes to the digital transformation of Ayurvedic healthcare services.
